I found a credible load-order failure candidate: if `engine-fast-worker-host.js` loads after `engine-fast-par-host.js`, the headless runner registration for `event-fast-par` can be overwritten and return a live engine instead of an async headless runner. I’m reproducing that exact scenario in Node before patching.
